The exact-context interceptor itself is what fails to match; the fixed `#loop` state is otherwise identical. I’m narrowing the mechanism: intercept only the exact `<k>` term, use the full proven transition only when the exact valid state also matches, and otherwise take a universal `owise` fallback that performs MPY’s first loop step. I’ll strengthen the fallback theorem to be context-universal, which fully justifies this broader interceptor.
